2026-09-09T05:00:00Z ADVANCED (outside /maker - the Stop hook caught it, correctly) - Umesh asked whether the loop was actually validating in a browser what it builds. It was not: ~19 units this session, browser opened zero times. Made live-browser validation MANDATORY across the shared skills (his call: all three maker-checker projects, not a KnowledgeBase-only override): maker cycle step 5b (browser BEFORE the manifest, gated on CHANGED PATHS not adapter.json, since KnowledgeBase and erp have no adapter.json and BOTH prior browser rules were dead here), a required "Live browser evidence" manifest section, checker Mode D (per-unit, pre-PASS, own browser, reading the maker's screenshots explicitly is NOT verification, INTERACTION required not rendering), a LIVE-BROWSER verdict field, and delivery-gate-stop.ps1 predicate BROWSER. Fixture-tested 5 ways. AIOS f339aaa + repo 3c61c77 (D-024). Also fixed the friction so the gate does not get switched off: PORT default 3000 -> 3300 (the bug the first browser run found: every web call ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED, dashboard dead, 9 console errors, invisible to unit tests because both sides were individually correct) and pnpm demo:up. THEN FIXED THE NODE-CLICK BUG Umesh found by hand, as the rule's first unit (de39232). The cause was mundane and nothing was broken in code: onNodeClick always fired when a click landed on a node, but only 1.2% of the canvas (32/2601 grid points, 5px radius, ~180 nodes) was ever over one, so a person aiming at a visible dot misses repeatedly. nodePointerAreaPaint gives a 10px screen-space target divided by globalScale; 8.8% after, 7.2x, dot size unchanged. TWO CORRECTIONS TO MY OWN CONFIDENT CLAIMS, both recorded in the evidence report and the inbox: "pointer picking never fires" came from polling canvas.style.cursor when force-graph signals hover with a `clickable` CSS CLASS, so every zero-hover reading measured NOTHING; and "the DPR scale is lost (0.913 vs 1.25)" was wrong because 0.9134/1.25 = 0.7308 is the zoom factor and the transform folds zoom in. Both changes made on that theory fixed nothing - the `key` remount is REVERTED (it would have reset the graph layout on every window resize for no benefit) and the rounding is kept as hygiene with a comment that claims no credit. Lesson filed: test the probe against a KNOWN-POSITIVE before reporting a negative. OWED, and it is my own FAIL: hybrid-arms-binding (U1.5 part 2) is at cycle 1 FAIL - ISS-169 (mutation K hoisting extraCandidateArmsFor("system") out of the request handler leaves 170/170 GREEN; the factory's internals are pinned, the BINDING SITE - C6's actual substance - is not) and ISS-170 (the 0.891 measures a near-neighbour policy: the eval's tree arm is createHeuristicRetriever, which its own header disclaims, while askV2 uses selectNodes, and the eval's lexical arm reads 20 turns where the shipped one reads 5 - so my headline diagnosis about "the tree arm voting with the authority of noise" is about an arm that does not ship). That is the next tick. The other two open manifests (speaker-verbatim-token-boundary, write-guard-enforcement-gaps) belong to other lanes.
